+// CLASSES, REFUSED: EVERY REFUSAL CYCLE 0.1.3 MAKES INSIDE A CLASS, WITH ITS OFFSET,
+// LENGTH AND DETAIL (`SYNTAX.md` §9's table, Y-36 … Y-38).
+//
+// Each case parses one pattern through `syntax.npk`'s re-exports and requires the
+// refusal to be EXACTLY this kind at this offset, spanning this many bytes, with this
+// detail -- the four fields a message is built from (Y-10, Y-34). A case that differs
+// exits with its number. An escape other than punctuation, a Perl class or a property
+// is refused PROVISIONALLY inside a class as outside it (Y-31) and is not pinned here:
+// cycle 0.1.4 changes it. `NestTooDeep` at a `[` is `parse_limits`' and
+// `parse_nest_deep`'s.
